Preventive care reduces the incidence of chronic diseases, which are often more expensive to treat over time.
Studies show that every dollar invested in preventive care can save up to $5 in future healthcare costs.
Early detection through screenings allows for less invasive and less costly treatment options.
Preventive measures like vaccinations prevent the spread of diseases, reducing overall healthcare system burden.
By avoiding severe complications, preventive care minimizes the need for long-term, expensive treatments.